From fee384e026c6c4a201b01b8120590d3ba918cd10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:47:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vc4: hvs6: Round up the LBM width of subsampled channels

vc4_lbm_channel_size() divided the width by the horizontal subsampling,
rounding down. A 1 pixel wide YUV source got no LBM at all, and odd
widths, such as 33 pixels upscaled, got a line too short, either of which
corrupts the next plane's LBM.

Signed-off-by: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_plane.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_plane.c
@@ -895,7 +895,7 @@ static unsigned int vc4_lbm_channel_size
 		width = state->crtc_w;
 	else
 		width = min(src_w, state->crtc_w);
-	width = round_up(width / info->hsub, 4);
+	width = round_up(DIV_ROUND_UP(width, info->hsub), 4);
 
 	wpc = vc4_lbm_words_per_component(state, channel);
 	if (!wpc)
